        <argsstring>(const MDNode &amp;FirstN)</argsstring>
        <name>mapTopLevelUniquedNode</name>
        <qualifiedname>anonymous_namespace{ValueMapper.cpp}::MDNodeMapper::mapTopLevelUniquedNode</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="_a_arch64_promote_constant_8cpp_1a90f8350fecae261c25be85d38b451bff" kindref="member">const</ref> <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_m_d_node" kindref="compound">MDNode</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>FirstN</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Map a top-level uniqued node and the uniqued subgraph underneath it. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This builds up a post-order traversal of the (unmapped) uniqued subgraph underneath <computeroutput>FirstN</computeroutput> and calculates the nodes&apos; mapping. Each node uses the identity mapping (<emphasis>Mapper::mapToSelf()</emphasis>) as long as all of its operands uses the identity mapping.</para>
<para>The algorithm works as follows:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><emphasis>createPOT()</emphasis>: traverse the uniqued subgraph under <computeroutput>FirstN</computeroutput> and save the post-order traversal in the given <emphasis>UniquedGraph</emphasis>, tracking nodes&apos; operands change.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><emphasis>UniquedGraph::propagateChanges()</emphasis>: propagate changed operands through the <emphasis>UniquedGraph</emphasis> until fixed point, following the rule that if a node changes, any node that references must also change.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><emphasis>mapNodesInPOT()</emphasis>: map the uniqued nodes, creating new uniqued nodes (referencing new operands) where necessary. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
