        <briefdescription>
<para>Try to map the operand of an <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_m_d_node" kindref="compound">MDNode</ref></emphasis>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacellvm_1ab471937b9a227e70c7fe8bd9604014d6" kindref="member">Op</ref></computeroutput> is already mapped, return the mapping. If it&apos;s not an <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_m_d_node" kindref="compound">MDNode</ref></emphasis>, compute and return the mapping. If it&apos;s a distinct <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_m_d_node" kindref="compound">MDNode</ref></emphasis>, return the result of <emphasis>mapDistinctNode()</emphasis>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>std::nullopt if <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacellvm_1ab471937b9a227e70c7fe8bd9604014d6" kindref="member">Op</ref></computeroutput> is an unmapped uniqued <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_m_d_node" kindref="compound">MDNode</ref></emphasis>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>getMappedOp(Op) only returns std::nullopt if this returns std::nullopt. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
