        <briefdescription>
<para>Create a post-order traversal of an unmapped uniqued node subgraph. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This traverses the metadata graph deeply enough to map <computeroutput>FirstN</computeroutput>. It uses <emphasis>tryToMapOperand()</emphasis> (via <emphasis>Mapper::mapSimplifiedNode()</emphasis>), so any metadata that has already been mapped will not be part of the POT.</para>
<para>Each node that has a changed operand from outside the graph (e.g., a distinct node, an already-mapped uniqued node, or <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_constant_as_metadata" kindref="compound">ConstantAsMetadata</ref></emphasis>) is marked with <emphasis>Data::HasChanged</emphasis>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if any nodes in <computeroutput>G</computeroutput> have <emphasis>Data::HasChanged</emphasis>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para><computeroutput>G.POT</computeroutput> is a post-order traversal ending with <computeroutput>FirstN</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para><emphasis>Data::hasChanged</emphasis> in <computeroutput>G.Info</computeroutput> indicates whether any node needs to change because of operands outside the graph. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
